{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/954800-making-a-birthright-to-channel-a-new-purview","id":954800,"title":"Making a Birthright to channel a new purview.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-20T21:20:37-07:00","id":954800,"title":"Making a Birthright to channel a new purview.","content":"how would it look mythologically, when you try learning a Purview that no god in your pantheon has an affinity for <br /> <br /> like non of the Jappanese pantheon have an affinity for Magic, mysterry or prophecy.<br /> <br /> any ideas how it will look making bargains with gods from other pantheons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:27:59-07:00","id":954823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/954800-making-a-birthright-to-channel-a-new-purview#post954800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how would it look mythologically, when you try learning a Purview that no god in your pantheon has an affinity for<br /> <br /> like non of the Jappanese pantheon have an affinity for Magic, mysterry or prophecy.<br /> <br /> any ideas how it will look making bargains with gods from other pantheons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends a lot on your Pantheon, your Pantheon's outlook on that Purview, and the Pantheon you are bartering with. Sort of a mess of possibilities, but that's the best sort of mess! Especially in Scion. I can give a few examples if that is helpful!<br /> <br /> <b>Example A</b>: A Tuatha Scion attempting to get a Frost Relic from the Aesir. (Using an Updated Tuatha Purview list)<br /> <br /> To start with, let's look at the Tuatha's outlook on Frost! It's pretty much non-existent. The Tuatha are not Elemental Forces like you get with the Greeks for example (save for the Land Goddesses, and a Goddess who turns into a river) and instead their Purviews are mostly expressions of their skills. Brigid has Fire through her Inspiration of the arts, Manannan has purview over the sea due to his father being the King of the Sea. (Manannan also has command of the winds through his sword) So, the Tuatha would be understanding to people who wield Purviews through Relics (Manannan's sword and Sky) so if one of the Scions appeared with something that gave them command of Winter and Ice, the Tuatha would be pleased! Look at the clever little Hero! They have traveled far afield and returned with a new Feat! One of ice, of winter, and cold. A terrible force to unleash upon their foes and kill their crops, freeze their rivers, and slaughter their cattle. (though they'd be happier if you could just <i>steal</i> the cattle instead)<br /> <br /> Now, the Aesir and the Tuatha get along fairly well, since the Tuatha <i>do not</i> have a great relationship with their Mortals who the Norse fought a bunch. If Skadi or Uller gave a Scion a spear tipped with a sliver of one of Ymir's bones, granting them access to the Frost Purview, that would go well! Other options include Runes, or perhaps marrying one of Skadi's siblings. (though that would be a round about way to access the Purview, and not actually a Relic) The Tuatha Scion would likely need to preform some deed, or impress Skadi or Uller to get such a gift, but for the Tuatha who being boisterous and brilliant is standard social practice, it could work!<br /> <br /> This is an example of a exceptionally positive exchange.<br /> <br /> <b>Example B</b>: A Netjer Scion getting a Darkness Relic from the Teotl.<br /> <br /> To start with, let's look at the Netjer's outlook on Darkness! It's <i>really really really bad</i>. While RAW stats Aten as the enemy of the Egyptian Pantheon, mythologically, the great enemy of the Pantheon is Apep, a great serpent attempting to devour the sun in its nightly passage through Duat. One of their Scions developing the Darkness Purview would be looked upon with extreme suspicion until details are learned. If they are wielding Darkness as a Nightime figure, a patron of some Nocturnal Owl, or perhaps as a kind benelovent Darkness figure giving the people refuge from the heat of the desert sun when away from the Nile, they would give you a pass. <i>But</i> if you were one of the Darkness-Overcoming-Light figures, you would likely be grabbed by the scruff of your neck and dragged before your Divine Parent who would tear into you. Your Virtues would also likely be screaming at you for this.<br /> <br /> Now, the Teotl and the Netjer don't have much contact, so as long as the Netjer Scion doesn't do anything that would upset the Pantheon, nothing much will come of this. (The Netjer and Teotl have a lot of similar values. Don't like the night, strict social stuff, regulated death systems, multi-part souls) But, the Teotl <i>hate</i> Darkness, in fact, you would be getting your Darkness Relic from The Black Tezcatlipoca, The Enemy of Both Sides. The God of the Night Sky and regular suspect when someone destroys the Sun, he would likely require you to do <i>something</i> that will further his aims which are likely not great. The task may just be large scale sacrifice for some sort of plot against his brother, or might intentionally provoke behavior that will be frowned upon by the Netjer. The greater Teotl Pantheon themselves however likely will keep a <i>very</i> close eye on this Scion from now on, ready to step in and end a threat to The Fifth Sun at any moment.<br /> <br /> This is an example of a really negative exchange.<br /> <br /> <b>Example C</b>: A Kami Scion gaining a Prophecy Relic from the Theoi.<br /> <br /> To start, let's look at the Kami's outlook on Prophecy. Now, they have a system of Prophecy, however it is detached from Fate (rather common really) and instead is a system of seeking interaction with various Kami to get their thoughts on matters. Sacerdos knows more about the nitty gritty specifics, but in the very least, they have a <i>very</i> different system of Fate than the Greeks, the closest possibly being Buddhist Karma, though that's a complicated area in how it relates to the Kami. So, Prophecy-As-The-Will-Of-Fate is rather alien.<br /> <br /> Now, the Theoi and the Kami likely have limited contact. However, both are Imperial Pantheons, so they would have similar-ish outlooks on the world. Up until the Theoi make sexist comments about Amaterasu ruling, botch social interactions, and the Pantheons argue about who'se Cosmology is correct. But, let's say they have had little direct contact due to the Theoi being mostly self-interested, and the Kami being insanely insular.<br /> <br /> Now, here's the complicated part. The ST has to deal with Clashing Cosmologies. The way I would rule it is, if the Kami Scion is using a Theoi Prophecy Relic (probably a three-legged stool, or a bottle of fumes from Python's corpse) they are accessing the Theoi concept of Prophecy. That is an all-powerful force that binds even Gods, Titans, and Primordials to its will which is outside their grasp. (except in some very Zeus-is-the-best-ever Cults) In this case, the Kami Scion is tapping into an alien force which would likely make the Kami <i>very</i> disappointed in you, and when they learned you were throwing around powers that could try (Cross-Cosmology stuff can be tricky to not make one more 'true' than another) to bend even them to its will, they would be annoyed. They might demand you never use it on one of the Amatsukami, and allow you to bully other, less important Kami and mortals with it. Or, they might discourage you using it through social pushback.<br /> <br /> If the Scion kept using the Prophecy Purview, and if they became Legend 9 with it as one of their key features, I would rule that there is Cultural Melding taking place, and I would slowly start to have the Moirae (who I might stat as Titans of a Fate Realm) interfering with Kami situations. What happens next is up to the Kami. Will they embrace this new, outside force and then probably claim it was theirs all along and, in fact, they gave it to the Theoi? Or will they push against it, fight the Moirae, and combat the young Deity who is bringing an invading, outside magic against them?<br /> <br /> That's an example of a really messy and complicated situation.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I hope that helps! If you have a specific Pantheon or Situation, I could provide more specific detail if you would like!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 08-21-2016, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:39:21-07:00","id":955094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/954800-making-a-birthright-to-channel-a-new-purview?p=954823#post954823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends a lot on your Pantheon, your Pantheon's outlook on that Purview, and the Pantheon you are bartering with. Sort of a mess of possibilities, but that's the best sort of mess! Especially in Scion. I can give a few examples if that is helpful!<br /> <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I hope that helps! <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna steal aaaaaaaall of that, Watcher. Shamelessly.<br /> <br /> &lt;3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}